255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Corporate social responsibility \(CSR\) policies of gold-mining production in Sudan offer an important and revealing lens through which to view the broader structural and political transformations in the country. By tracing the successive stages of the CSR experience, the contours of these structural and political shifts, especially after the December 2018 Revolution, become clear. This study demonstrates the significance of CSR policies as an expression of the state's turn toward market-oriented policies, reflecting a broader regional and global transformation that followed the era of developmental states up to the 1970s and the subsequent shifts that came after.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
